WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.626 --> 00:00:01.877
- I'm a Jew.

00:00:01.877 --> 00:00:04.083
So I don't have a lot of
experience with bacon.

00:00:04.083 --> 00:00:06.173
So this is going to be
my little Jewish cheat.

00:00:06.719 --> 00:00:09.319
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.596 --> 00:00:13.097
- Wow, these are thick!

00:00:13.097 --> 00:00:15.517
- It lacks the crispness that I've seen

00:00:15.517 --> 00:00:17.059
in pictures of bacon.

00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:18.369
Which just makes it
seem like that I'm just

00:00:18.369 --> 00:00:20.483
at my computer looking
at pictures of bacon,

00:00:20.483 --> 00:00:21.480
like, crying.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.324
- It tastes like you're eating a tire.

00:00:23.324 --> 00:00:24.233
- It's a good alternative.

00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:26.652
I guess like the best
alternative is no bacon.

00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:28.279
- When I'm trying to be healthy,

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:30.364
or I'm like getting my
body the right stuff,

00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:31.571
this is what I eat.

00:00:33.951 --> 00:00:35.252
- Chicken bacon?

00:00:35.252 --> 00:00:36.236
- That exists?

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.871
- For some reason I'm getting

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.581
like a tennis ball vibe from this.

00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:40.624
I don't know why.

00:00:40.624 --> 00:00:43.085
- This is fantastic, this is
better than my mom's bacon.

00:00:43.085 --> 00:00:44.420
Don't tell her about that.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.632
- That weird aftertaste,
though. What is that?

00:00:46.632 --> 00:00:47.881
- What did they put in it?

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.882
Like, how do they do this?

00:00:50.856 --> 00:00:52.052
- Just chicken?

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.179
- You're just trying to be
like, "Aren't I crunchy?"

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:56.933
Here's what happened: you
went for crunch over taste.

00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:58.332
That was not a good idea.

00:01:01.862 --> 00:01:03.362
- What?

00:01:03.562 --> 00:01:05.309
This doesn't smell anything like bacon.

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:07.860
- This one, it looks like a dinosaur.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.109
Or like some kind of
seahorse or something.

00:01:10.989 --> 00:01:13.345
- Uh! It's hard to pull, sorry.

00:01:13.345 --> 00:01:17.078
- Dude... this is so good.

00:01:17.078 --> 00:01:19.246
- It's fine, it tastes like beef jerky.

00:01:19.246 --> 00:01:20.645
We're going to stop by the gas station

00:01:20.645 --> 00:01:22.514
and pick this up on the way to Disneyland?

00:01:22.514 --> 00:01:23.522
Cool.

00:01:23.522 --> 00:01:24.567
- I'll allow this.

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.077
This is the only other bacon I'll allow.

00:01:28.547 --> 00:01:30.001
- Uh, lamb bacon?

00:01:31.403 --> 00:01:33.845
- Ew, oh no!

00:01:34.235 --> 00:01:36.129
I love Lamb Chop!

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.047
- It looks like I'm
going to have diarrhea.

00:01:38.047 --> 00:01:39.099
Instantly.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.476
- Oh, God no.

00:01:40.476 --> 00:01:42.770
Oh, oh, what's going on with this one?

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:44.563
- Look at how much fat it is.

00:01:44.563 --> 00:01:46.695
- All the fat just turns into like liquid,

00:01:46.695 --> 00:01:47.816
instantly, in your mouth.

00:01:47.816 --> 00:01:48.776
It's weird.

00:01:48.776 --> 00:01:50.748
- I just ate Lamb Chop!

00:01:54.907 --> 00:01:57.201
- Dude, what is this?

00:01:57.201 --> 00:01:59.370
- It feels like an emoji bacon.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.039
- Are you even trying?

00:02:01.039 --> 00:02:02.998
This looks like a fruit rollup.

00:02:02.998 --> 00:02:04.750
- Ooh, I like that.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.752
- This is something you
get in elementary school

00:02:06.752 --> 00:02:09.088
to, like, put inside your book.

00:02:09.088 --> 00:02:11.673
- This is like one of those slap bracelets

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:12.966
that you put on your arm.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.093
Oh, I broke it!

00:02:14.093 --> 00:02:16.595
- My dad used to make us eat these.

00:02:16.595 --> 00:02:19.181
And I was like, I'm going to
convert away from Judaism.

00:02:19.181 --> 00:02:21.350
- But like it's good, like it's okay.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:24.520
I wouldn't kick it out of
bed for eating crackers.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.980
- Turkey bacon is still the best one.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.683
And I don't even really eat meat anymore,

00:02:28.683 --> 00:02:31.149
and I'll tell you,
turkey bacon is the boo.

00:02:31.819 --> 00:02:33.491
It will never be beat.

00:02:33.821 --> 00:02:34.988
I went to a Jewish dayschool and I

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:36.574
had a teacher one time tell me that

00:02:36.574 --> 00:02:38.622
I shouldn't even eat turkey bacon

00:02:38.622 --> 00:02:40.921
because another Jew might see me eat it

00:02:40.921 --> 00:02:43.540
and be like, "Oh, no,
she's allowed to eat bacon,

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:44.957
"why aren't I allowed to eat bacon?"

00:02:44.957 --> 00:02:46.491
And then all of Judaism would collapse.

